// ENCODER CROSS-LINGUAL PROBES — IT/EN translation pairs for the recall@1 half of the encoder gate
// (tools/anima-host/enc-quality.mjs). The encoder is distilled BILINGUAL: an EN question and its IT
// translation are supposed to land in the same place in the embedding space. We score that the way
// distill.py does at training time — for every EN probe, its own IT translation must be the nearest
// of ALL the IT probes — but here against the SHIPPED weights, so a bad export can't slip through.
//
// Topics are deliberately spread out: near-duplicate probes would make recall@1 easy for the wrong
// reason (nothing to confuse them with) instead of measuring cross-lingual alignment.
//
// Fields: it, en.
